{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1564794-reverse-engineering-ambrosia","id":1564794,"title":"Reverse engineering Ambrosia","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-10-16T18:59:46-07:00","id":1564794,"title":"Reverse engineering Ambrosia","content":"How hard would it be for a superintelligent crafting-focused Nova or other mad scientist type (particularly in later eras, when the science in understood better) to reverse engineer the Ambrosia that gave the Aegis era characters their powers? That is, create a serum that fairly reliably Inspires people into all three classes of Inspired.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25249-deathbyflossing","name":"deathbyflossing","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-16T19:11:49-07:00","id":1564795,"title":"","content":"That\u2019s a great idea! I don\u2019t think it would be difficult at all for an Inspired with a scientific bent from any of the three classes (psiads, novas or Talents) to rediscover the secret of ambrosia in the Aberrant era (circa 2028) or later eras.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-17T08:38:50-07:00","id":1564803,"title":"","content":"For a high mega-int nova? Probably doable, but you'll need to be later on in the Nova age, given that at least at game start nanotechnology is still in a very early experimental stage, so accessing the tools to develop it would likely be difficult. You're also running into the difficulty that you don't know psiads are a thing, and nova tech generally can't interact on the noetic level. That said, they can probably brute force replicating it at least.<br /> <br /> For talents and psiads/psions? Not during their game line periods. They don't have the level of intelligence boosting Novas do, so they can't brute-force the scientific understanding, and they don't have the theoretical basis in various power types to figure what's going on. Psions can't even figure out most Nova tech, nor can they figure out the more simple psion-specific empowerment tech in thr form of Prometheus Chambers. It'd probably take at least a century of dedicated research to reach the point they can understand Ambrosia.<br /> <br /> Now, if you pair up a Banru and Eden research team, then they can probably make it work within a decade, probably less.<br /> <br /> Of course, this comes with the caveat that nobody has a clue as to what Talents are, so you're going to need to hope you get access to those by accident.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28973-kenod","name":"kenod","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-17T12:36:20-07:00","id":1564804,"title":"","content":"The Nova offering the Ambrosia should set himself up as a opposite to Divis Mal. Divis Mal wants Novas to be gods above mortals. This new guy (let's call him Prometheus..&quot;stealing fire from heaven&quot;) wants mortals to become godlike. Divis Mal might respect that, but most of the Terragen would be furious.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}